## Decision rule

Classification is necessary for promotion rule 3; it is not sufficient. Record design class, replication of the *narrow* claim, and GI attenuation (largely confounded >50% / partial 20–50% / robust <20% / n/a / not classified). Grey-lit IDs are framework, not identification.

## Stable-candidate note

Before any `status: stable` flip, write or extend `stable-candidates--replication-note.md` with a five-rule table per card. Number waves explicitly (`# First wave`, `# Second wave`) so later entries are not an orphaned 4–7. Historical non-promotions stay historically accurate; a later wave may supersede a named hold.

Promote the *narrow* High claim only. Independent conceptual replication must be on the card (different lab or a meta of the procedure), not a neighboring identification.

## YAML vs prose

If YAML `confidence` or `description` diverges from the body or the primary paper, align YAML to the paper. A YAML fix is not a second experiment and does not by itself promote the card.

## Manuscript-revision checklist

When a pass touches curated `chapters/`:

- [ ] Archival `preliminary/drafts-chapters/` untouched
- [ ] Sleep / attachment-intervention / screen *theory* not rewritten
- [ ] Named card IDs match live filenames
- [ ] Cross-chapter terms (regulation, causation, risk, resilience, attachment, institutions) are not silently re-estimated
- [ ] Appendix B lengths preserved; Ch. 2 not padded
- [ ] CHANGELOG, index, MANIFEST, REPO_DIGEST, SOURCES updated together
- [ ] No new cards or chapters unless the user asked

Do not tag `v0.x` from a deepening pass unless a matching `preliminary/releases/v0.x-slice.md` exists.
